**Count:** 25 fine-grained slots (as-built).

## Optional coarse fold sketch (future only)

| Coarse domain (plan §2.3) | Candidate fine slots | Fold only when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `tourCreation` / `forms` | `createChrome`, `flatEditChrome`, `createView`, `flatEditForm`, `flatEditPage`, `wizardCreate`, parts of `draftShell` | Single call-graph owner + zero hydration regressions |
| `settings` | `settingsHubFallback`, `settingsDestination`, `settingsEquipmentUi`, `settingsExposureSurfacesUi`, `templateEditor`, `templatePreset`, `templateGate` | Settings hub no longer warms slots independently |
| `ops` | `financeNav`, `financeOps`, `bookingOps` | Dual-SOT derivation (4bu+) already green for all three |
| `navigation` | `operatorShellNav` (+ future nav slots) | More than one nav capability exists |
| `messages` / labels | `labels`, wizard i18n allowlist (not a capability) | Do **not** fold opaque §2.4 i18n into the bag |

```text
fine slots (locked now)
        │
        ▼  Architect YES + migration plan
coarse domain object on capabilities
        │
        ▼
shell resolvers updated; fine keys deprecated then removed
```

## Rules

1. **Default:** keep fine-grained; new surfaces add a new slot (or extend the nearest Pattern A/B slot).
2. **Fold requires Architect YES** plus: SDK doc, dual-publish window, arch tests updated in the same PR.
3. **Forbidden:** mega-refactor “to match the plan diagram”; deleting slots to chase hostile score; folding Pattern B React warm into coarse bags without Map keying.
4. **Orthogonal:** Dual-SOT (`thin-shell-dual-sot-derivation.mdoc`) and Pattern B Maps (`thin-shell-pattern-b-registry.mdoc`) — consolidation does not reopen those.

